## 14. Expected Outcome

The Privacy Impact Assessment identifies several potential privacy risks associated with a digital attendance management system, including unauthorized access, data breaches, excessive data collection, inappropriate use, biometric risks, and excessive data retention.

Implementing access controls, encryption, data minimization, secure authentication, retention policies, auditing, and privacy awareness can significantly reduce these risks.

## 15. Conclusion

A College Attendance Management System can make attendance management faster, more accurate, and more convenient. However, because the system processes students' personal information, privacy must be considered throughout its design and operation.

A Privacy Impact Assessment provides a systematic method for identifying privacy risks and developing appropriate safeguards. By applying privacy-by-design principles, limiting data collection, controlling access, securing stored information, and establishing appropriate retention and incident-response procedures, the college can reduce privacy risks while continuing to benefit from digital attendance management.

Therefore, conducting a PIA before implementing or significantly changing the system is an important step toward responsible management of students' personal information.
